REM  yadein.pni — the record.  یادیں
REM  THIS IS SOMEBODY'S LIFE, so the default inverts: nothing publishes
REM  unless that entry was marked for it, one entry at a time.

CYCLER YADEIN
  TITLE   "Yadein"
  SCRIPT  "یادیں"
  OUTPUT  RECORD
  UNIT    "entry"
  PURPOSE "Keep a life: a diary, an oral history, a family archive, a research notebook, a longitudinal record accumulated in fragments over years."

  CONTRACT
    REFUSE    "publishing any entry that was not individually marked"
    REFUSE    "sharpening a vague date into a precise one"
    REFUSE    "adding a surname, role or relationship the source never gave"
    REFUSE    "drawing a lesson where only a record was asked for"
    INVARIANT "the count withheld is recorded; the content withheld is not"
    INVARIANT "marking every entry private is a valid outcome, not an error"
    EVIDENCE  "an explicit mark per entry"
  END CONTRACT

  STAGE ENTRIES
    RESOLUTION EASY
    VERB   CREATE
    EXPECT LIST
    INTO   entries
    ASK
      Material for a record, "{book}". Separate it into entries.

      Reply with ONLY a JSON array, in the order things HAPPENED — which may not be the
      order they were written:
      [{"when":"1994-08","title":"…","beat":"…"}]

      when: as precise as the material actually supports. "1994", "1994-08",
      "some summer in the nineties". Do NOT sharpen a vague date into a precise one.
    END ASK
    VALIDATE COUNT(entries) > 0
  END STAGE

  STAGE HAPPENED
    RESOLUTION EASY
    VERB   CREATE
    EXPECT TEXT
    REPEAT FOREACH entries
    INTO   entry.lead
    ASK
      Entry {entry.title}, {entry.when}.

      ONE paragraph of 50 to 110 words recording what happened, in the words the material
      uses. Record it; do not interpret it, do not draw a lesson from it, and do not add a
      detail the material does not contain. Where the material is uncertain, keep the
      uncertainty.
    END ASK
  END STAGE

  STAGE HOLD
    RESOLUTION MID
    VERB   CREATE
    EXPECT TEXT
    FROM   entry.lead
    INTO   entry.hold
    ASK
      Same entry. In 40 to 90 words, name what is worth holding on to here and why — a
      fact, a face, a decision, a turning. This is the part a later reader, or a later
      you, would want kept.
    END ASK
  END STAGE

  STAGE WHO
    RESOLUTION MID
    VERB   CREATE
    EXPECT JSON
    INTO   entry.people
    ASK
      Same entry. Reply with ONLY:
      {"people":["…"],"places":["…"],"topics":["…"]}

      people: named ONLY as the material names them. Do not add surnames, roles or
      relationships it does not state. If someone is unnamed there, leave them unnamed here.
    END ASK
  END STAGE

  STAGE ATTACH
    RESOLUTION PRO
    VERB   INTEGRATE
    EXPECT ANY
    OPTIONAL
    ATTACH INBOX
    ASK
      Find what belongs with entry {entry.title} — a photograph, a voice note, a scan,
      a document. This is not generated. It already exists. Bring it and pick it out.
    END ASK
  END STAGE

  STAGE MARK
    RESOLUTION EASY
    VERB   VERIFY
    GATE   HUMAN "MARK entries"
    ENVELOPE "nothing publishes until every entry carries a mark, and all-private is a valid answer"
  END STAGE

  STAGE ABSTRACT
    RESOLUTION MID
    VERB   INTEGRATE
    EXPECT TEXT
    FROM   entries
    INTO   book.description
    ASK
      Deposit abstract for "{book}", a record in {count} entries.
      Two or three HTML paragraphs in <p> tags.
    END ASK
  END STAGE

  STAGE EXPORT
    RESOLUTION PRO
    VERB  INTEGRATE
    GATE  HUMAN "EXPORT yadein"
    EMIT  REPO
  END STAGE
END CYCLER
